   "en": "Hong Kong stocks rose on Monday, with the Hang Seng Index up 118 points, or 0.5%, at 23,211 on turnover of HK$175.8 billion. The Hang Seng Tech Index slipped 0.4% to 3,857, though its losses narrowed; the Shanghai Composite gained 0.2% to 3,697 and the Shenzhen Component fell 1.2% to 11,534. Investors are watching central bank interest rate decisions later this week. It is a bit like the day before an exam: people hold back from big bets until they see the questions."
