   "en": "Late Sunday, Dow futures were up about 0.22% and S&P 500 futures about 0.11%, while Nasdaq-100 futures were roughly flat. On Friday the Dow fell 1.23% to 52,215.16 and the S&P 500 lost 0.52% to 7,623.68, its second straight weekly decline, as tech and AI stocks weakened on worries about AI sustainability and debt. Brent was about US$114.85, off its highs, and the 10-year Treasury yield eased to 4.966%. Alphabet, Microsoft, Amazon, Visa and Boeing report this week, and the Fed begins its meeting Tuesday with markets largely expecting rates to hold. It is something like exam week: earnings and the central bank both post results at once."
