  "title": {
   "zh": "科技股重挫:Meta下跌约7%,半导体指数暴跌6.7%",
   "en": "Tech sinks Wall Street: Meta falls about 7% and chip index plunges 6.7%"
  },
  "analysis": {
   "zh": "周四纳指下跌2.60%至26,008.86点,为6月初以来最大单日跌幅;标普500跌1.21%至7,663.43点,道指微涨0.02%至52,867.98点。Meta业绩超预期,但公司出现十多年来首次现金净流出,股价跌约7%;费城半导体指数跌6.7%,英特尔、超威半导体等多只芯片股跌幅超过8%。分析人士称,投资者开始发现AI故事中的一些漏洞。这就像一场热闹的派对,大家忽然开始算账单:好故事还在,但价格要重新衡量。",
   "en": "On Thursday the Nasdaq Composite fell 2.60% to 26,008.86, its steepest daily drop since early June; the S&P 500 lost 1.21% to 7,663.43 and the Dow edged up 0.02% to 52,867.98. Meta beat estimates but posted its first cash outflow in over a decade and fell about 7%, while the Philadelphia semiconductor index dropped 6.7%, with Intel and AMD each down more than 8%. One strategist said investors are starting to see holes in the AI story. It's like a lively party where guests suddenly start checking the bill: the story is still there, but the price needs a fresh look."
  },
  "dda": {
   "zh": "科技股大幅回调时,定期定额的好处在于不需要判断底部;每月固定投入,价格较低时自然买到较多单位,长期有助摊平平均成本。",
   "en": "When tech pulls back sharply, the benefit of regular investing is that you don't have to call the bottom; a fixed monthly amount buys more units when prices are lower, which helps smooth your average cost over time."
  },
  "prs": {
   "zh": "退休规划是二三十年的旅程,一次科技股回调不会决定结果。可以趁机检查PRS基金的资产分布是否与年龄相符,每年供款最高RM3,000还可享个人税务减免。",
   "en": "Retirement planning is a 20-to-30-year journey, and one tech pullback doesn't decide the outcome. It's a good moment to check whether your PRS fund's asset mix suits your age; contributions of up to RM3,000 a year also qualify for personal tax relief."
  },
  "lump": {
   "zh": "当少数科技巨头带动大市升跌时,单笔投资要留意集中度。分阶段投入可以分散时间点风险,同时确认配置与目标和风险承受度相符。",
   "en": "When a few tech giants drive the market's ups and downs, a lump sum calls for a concentration check. Phasing in can spread timing risk, and it's worth confirming the mix matches your goals and risk tolerance."
  },
  "bond": {
   "zh": "股市下跌时资金常流向国债,美国收益率回落有时会令外资对新兴市场债券的压力减轻,对令吉也可能较友好。大马债券基金(马来西亚政府债券与企业债券、伊斯兰债券)一般能在股市波动时起到平衡组合的作用。",
   "en": "When stocks fall, money often moves into government bonds, and lower US yields can sometimes ease pressure on emerging-market bonds and be friendlier to the ringgit. Malaysian bond funds (MGS, corporate bonds and sukuk) generally help balance a portfolio when equities swing."
  },
