  "title": {
   "zh": "台股收跌1.81%,加权指数回落至46,041点",
   "en": "Taiwan shares close down 1.81% to 46,041"
  },
  "analysis": {
   "zh": "台湾加权指数周四下跌846.34点或1.81%,收46,041.43点,成交额为新台币8,792.3亿元。报道没有说明下跌原因,但同日美国费城半导体指数暴跌6.7%,亚洲科技股整体承压。这就像坐跷跷板,台股高度依赖芯片,往往跟着全球科技情绪一起上下。",
   "en": "Taiwan's benchmark index fell 846.34 points, or 1.81%, on Thursday to close at 46,041.43 on turnover of NT$879.23 billion. The report doesn't give a cause, but the same day the Philadelphia semiconductor index plunged 6.7% in the US, and Asian tech came under pressure. Like a seesaw, Taiwan's chip-heavy market tends to move with global tech sentiment."
  },
  "dda": {
   "zh": "单一市场或行业的波动,正是用基金分散投资的原因。定期定额投资全球或亚洲基金时,不必为了半导体的一天走势而改变计划。",
   "en": "Swings in a single market or industry are exactly why people use funds to diversify. If you invest regularly in global or Asian funds, there's usually no need to change the plan over one day of chip moves."
  },
  "prs": {
   "zh": "长期的退休基金往往已经包含科技类资产。关键是回头看整体配置是否过度偏重某一行业,并按年龄和退休时间表适时调整。",
   "en": "A long-term retirement fund often already holds technology exposure. The key is to look at whether the overall mix leans too heavily on one industry and adjust over time to your age and retirement timeline."
  },
  "lump": {
   "zh": "半导体股涨跌幅度大,若手上有一笔资金,要留意是否集中在单一主题。分阶段投入可以分散时间点风险,并先确认风险承受度。",
   "en": "Semiconductor stocks swing widely, so with a lump sum it pays to check you aren't concentrated in a single theme. Phasing in can spread timing risk, and it helps to confirm your risk tolerance first."
  },
  "bond": {
   "zh": "台股回落对大马债券基金没有直接影响,但全球风险情绪转弱时,资金可能流向较安全的资产。债券基金在组合中一般扮演平衡者的角色,减少整体波动。",
   "en": "Taiwan's pullback has no direct effect on Malaysian bond funds, but when global risk appetite weakens, money may move to safer assets. Bond funds generally play the role of a portfolio balancer, helping to reduce overall volatility."
  },
  "source": {
   "name": "Focus Taiwan",
   "url": "https://focustaiwan.tw/business/202610220008"
  }
