  "analysis": {
   "zh": "周二亚洲早盘,现货金跌0.3%至每盎司4,126.84美元,12月期金跌0.3%至4,146美元。投资者在等美联储10月27至28日的议息会议和下周的PCE通胀数据。美联储9月已加息25个基点至3.75%至4.00%;CME FedWatch显示下周维持利率不变的概率为83%,市场对12月加息的预期达94%。利率越高,持有不付利息的黄金的机会成本就越高。",
   "en": "In early Asian trade on Tuesday, spot gold fell 0.3% to $4,126.84 an ounce and December futures dropped 0.3% to $4,146. Investors are waiting for the Fed's October 27-28 meeting and next week's PCE inflation data. The Fed raised rates by 25 basis points in September to 3.75%-4.00%; CME FedWatch shows an 83% chance of no change next week, and expectations of a December hike stand at 94%. Higher rates raise the opportunity cost of holding gold, which pays no interest."
  },
  "dda": {
   "zh": "金价跟着利率预期上下,短期很难预测。若通过定期定额投资含黄金或大宗商品的基金,重点是长期纪律,而不是每天看金价。",
   "en": "Gold moves with rate expectations and is hard to predict in the short run. If you invest regularly in a fund that holds gold or commodities, the key is long-term discipline rather than watching the daily price."
  },
  "prs": {
   "zh": "黄金在退休组合中通常扮演分散风险的角色,而不是主要的增长来源。PRS基金本身已有资产配置,一般不需要因为金价一时的涨跌而改变供款计划。",
   "en": "In a retirement portfolio, gold usually plays a diversifying role rather than being the main source of growth. PRS funds already have their own asset mix, so there's generally no need to change your contribution plan because of a short-term move in gold."
  },
  "lump": {
   "zh": "金价处于4,100美元以上的高位,加上利率可能再升,单笔投入黄金相关资产的时间点风险较大。可以考虑分阶段投入,并留意黄金在整体组合中的比重是否过高。",
   "en": "With gold above $4,100 and rates possibly heading higher, timing risk is significant for a lump sum into gold-related assets. Consider phasing in, and keep an eye on whether gold is taking up too large a share of the overall portfolio."
  },
  "bond": {
   "zh": "美国加息预期升温,通常会让全球债券收益率维持在较高水平。对马来西亚债券基金来说,较高的收益率意味着新买入的债券收益较好,但现有债券的价格可能承压。国家银行的OPR决定和令吉走势也会影响本地债券表现。",
   "en": "Rising expectations of US rate hikes usually keep global bond yields high. For Malaysian bond funds, higher yields mean better income on newly bought bonds, though prices of existing bonds may come under pressure. Bank Negara's OPR decisions and the ringgit also shape local bond returns."
  },
  "source": {
   "name": "Investing.com",
   "url": "https://www.investing.com/news/economy-news/gold-slips-as-investors-weigh-fed-rate-outlook-4958646"
  }
