   "en": "The Taiex closed Wednesday at 46,887.77, up 594.84 points (1.28%) after Tuesday's 1.13% fall. Super Micro Computer raised its sales forecast, lifting Hon Hai 3.52% and Quanta 1.25%, while TSMC rose 0.62% to NT$2,420. Analysts noted turnover did not expand much and the index stayed below 47,000 as investors wait for more AI signals. Like changeable weather, short-term swings are normal; the longer trend matters more."
