   "en": "Investing.com reports Brent futures fell 1.4% to $108.35 a barrel in early Monday trade after jumping nearly 5% last week. Trump signed an order suspending many Russia sanctions just before they took effect and waived tariffs on buyers of Russian oil, so markets are positioning for better supply, though Middle East tensions, including the US-Iran standoff and Saudi-Houthi clashes, still support prices. Oil is like a pipe running through every commodity: when the valve moves, transport and everyday costs feel it."
