   "en": "The Star reports the FBM KLCI closed Friday at 1,607.76, down 15.94 points (0.98%) and 0.63% lower on the week, while Malaysia's 3Q GDP advance estimate of 5.3% (6% in the previous quarter) exceeded expectations. The ringgit slipped 0.01% to 4.0822 against the US dollar, and foreign and local institutions were net sellers on Thursday. A strong report card meeting a falling market is like good exam results on a rainy day: short-term mood does not always follow the data."
