   "en": "Yahoo Finance reports US September CPI rose 3.7% year on year, above the 3.6% expected, with core CPI at 2.6% versus 2.5% expected. The 10-year Treasury yield rose more than 6 basis points to about 5.278% as investors worried the Fed could hike again this month. It is a bit like a higher utility bill: households start re-working their budgets."
