   "en": "Yahoo Finance reports that China's largest memory maker CXMT said it has progressed on a denser 4F² memory-cell design and aims to ship server memory built on it by year-end. The Kospi fell almost 5% to about 6,100 in Tuesday morning trade, with Samsung and SK Hynix each down roughly 5%; the two make up more than half of the index's value. One analyst expects dip-buying could spark a rebound. It is like a long-established shop seeing a new rival open across the road: the threat may not arrive at once, but the market gets nervous first."
