   "en": "Yahoo Finance reports Brent fell $1.62 to $105.03 and WTI to $92.08 in early Tuesday trade after President Trump said Russia agreed to raise diesel supplies, though analysts doubt its refiners can deliver. Meanwhile Houthi forces reportedly attacked Riyadh's airport and tanker incidents were reported near the Strait of Hormuz, with shipping and insurance costs at record levels. OPEC also cut its 2026 demand-growth forecast to 400,000 barrels a day. Oil is like the household utility bill: its moves feed into many other costs."
